.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs programs written in Wattle,
a Lisp-like programming language.
Wattle reimplements the virtual machine,
compiler and core library from the Janet programming language
in Zig with a syntax inspired by Clojure.
See
.Xr wattle 7
for more details on the language itself.
.Pp
.Nm
has seven subcommands:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Cm apps
- manages installed applications
.It
.Cm build
- builds a project artifacts
.It
.Cm check
- checks a file without running it
.It
.Cm deps
- manages the dependencies of a project
.It
.Cm gum
- copies Gum modules into a project
.It
.Cm run
- runs a script,
evaluates code or starts a REPL
.It
.Cm test
- runs the tests of a project
.El
.Pp
A user can run
.Ql "wattle help <subcommand>"
for more information about a subcommand.
.Pp
The default subcommand is
.Cm run .
As a result,
this:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle
$ wattle hello\&.wattle
$ wattle -e \(aq\*(lp+ 1 2\*(rp\(aq
.Ed
.Pp
is equivalent to:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle run
$ wattle run hello\&.wattle
$ wattle run -e \(aq\*(lp+ 1 2\*(rp\(aq
.Ed
.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl c ,
.Fl "-color"
.Xc
Enables ANSI colour for writing to stderr and stdout.
If
.Fl C
is also given,
.Fl C
applies.
.It Xo
.Fl C ,
.Fl "-no-color"
.Xc
Disables ANSI color for writing to stderr and stdout.
.It Xo
.Fl p ,
.Fl "-prefix"
.Ar path
.Xc
Sets the root directory from which
.Ql "lib/wattle" ,
.Ql "bin"
and
.Ql "share/man"
derive.
This replaces the value taken from
.Ev WATTLE_PREFIX .
.It Xo
.Fl v ,
.Fl "-version"
.Xc
Prints the version of Wattle and exits.
.It Xo
.Fl h ,
.Fl "-help"
.Xc
Prints a usage summary and exits.
Each subcommand supports
.Fl h ,
and prints its own usage.
.El
.
