.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ev WATTLE_PREFIX
.Xc
The directory that is used to set the dynamic binding
.Ql "*prefix*" .
This binding is used to derive the binpath,
the libpath and the manpath.
The binpath is
.Ql "<prefix>/bin"
and is the location into which executables are installed.
The libpath is
.Ql "<prefix>/lib/wattle"
and is the location into which applications are installed.
It is not searched by
.Ql "import" .
The manpath is
.Ql "<prefix>/share/man"
and is the location into which man pages are installed.
It can be overridden by
.Fl "-prefix" .
.Nm
can run without a value for
.Ql "*prefix*"
being set but it will exit with an error if a user tries to
use binpath,
libpath and manpath.
.It Xo
.Ev WATTLE_HISTFILE
.Xc
A file to record the history of commands sent to the REPL.
See
.Xr wattle-run 1 .
.It Xo
.Ev NO_COLOR
.Xc
If set to a non-empty value,
disable colour.
Colour is otherwise used when both standard output and standard
error are terminals.
.It Xo
.Ev TERM ,
.Ev COLORTERM
.Xc
The terminal has 256 colours if
.Ev TERM
contains
.Ql "256color"
or
.Ev COLORTERM
is set to a non-empty value,
and 16 otherwise.
.El
.Pp
An environment variable set to the empty string is treated as
unset.
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits
.Ql "0"
on success and
.Ql "1"
if a script,
a subcommand or an option raises an error that is not handled.
An error in the REPL is printed and does not end the session.
A program can set its own status with
.Ql "\*(lpos/exit status\*(rp" .
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the REPL,
run a script and evaluate an expression:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle
$ wattle hello\&.wattle Alice Bob
$ wattle -e \(aq\*(lpprint \*(lp+ 1 2 3\*(rp\*(rp\(aq
.Ed
.Pp
Each subcommand’s page has further examples.
.
